## External tools (subprocess only — not linked / not imported)

### gallery-dl — `core/udl/extractors/external/gallerydl.py`
- Upstream: https://github.com/mikf/gallery-dl
- License: **GPL-2.0-only** (LICENSE is GPLv2; source headers say
  "GNU General Public License version 2" — **not** or-later)
- Verified commit: 7f226f74108501c8ac3120548370f68f19e6f9b3 (v1.32.17)
- **Decision:** Incompatible with linking/importing into this GPL-3.0-or-later
  process. Integrate **only** as a separate subprocess (`gallery-dl` executable
  or `python -m gallery_dl`), communicating via CLI/JSON (`-j`/`--dump-json`,
  `-s`/`--simulate`, `--Print`, `--cookies`, `--proxy`, `--limit-rate`,
  `--download-archive`, `-o` options). Do **not** vendor or `import gallery_dl`.
- Redistribution: release builds may **bundle a separate gallery-dl binary**
  produced by PyInstaller (mere aggregation). Accompanying files:
  `packaging/gallery-dl/LICENSE.gallery-dl` and `SOURCE.txt` (upstream URL +
  commit). Users may instead install gallery-dl themselves
  (`pip`/`uv`/`brew`) and set Settings → gallery-dl path or `UDL_GALLERY_DL`.
- Router priority: after native Gofile/Bunkr/Iwara/Bilibili/MEGA, before
  generic `direct`. Matching uses gallery-dl’s own URL recognition (`-E`).
- Auth: cookies file and/or `udl.secrets` keys `gallerydl.username` /
  `gallerydl.password` (optional per-site
  `gallerydl.username.<category>`). Secrets are never logged.
- Explicitly **not** implemented: paywall/quota/DRM bypass; Cloudflare
  challenge bypass stays opt-in / off by default (no automatic bypass).

### MEGA external fallback — `core/udl/extractors/external/mega.py`
