## Bundled / first-run FFmpeg downloads

The desktop app may download a **static FFmpeg binary** on first use when none
is found on PATH / `UDL_FFMPEG` / Settings. Builds are checksum-verified before
install into the application data directory (`…/ffmpeg/`).

### Windows x64 — BtbN FFmpeg-Builds (LGPL static)
- Source: https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds
- Asset: `ffmpeg-master-latest-win64-lgpl.zip` from the `latest` release
- Checksum: verified against the release `checksums.sha256` at download time
- License: **LGPL** variant (non-GPL build). FFmpeg itself is LGPL 2.1+ /
  GPL 2+ depending on configure options; this asset is the LGPL build.

### macOS arm64 — Martin Riedl static builds
- Source: https://ffmpeg.martin-riedl.de/
- Asset: `redirect/latest/macos/arm64/release/ffmpeg.zip`
- Checksum: verified against the companion `ffmpeg.zip.sha256` next to the
  resolved download URL
- License: these builds typically enable GPL components (e.g. x264/x265).
  Treat the downloaded macOS binary as **GPL** unless you replace it with an
  LGPL-only build. See https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html.

Users may instead install FFmpeg themselves and point Settings → FFmpeg path
(or set `UDL_FFMPEG`). This project does not redistribute FFmpeg inside the
signed/unsigned app bundle by default; the optional download is user-initiated.

## Design inspiration (Unlicense — not a port of upstream code)

### yt-dlp lazy extractor registry — `scripts/make_lazy_extractors.py`,
`core/udl/extractors/lazy_load.py`, `core/udl/extractors/lazy_extractors.py`
- Upstream: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
- License: **Unlicense** (public domain dedication)
- Referenced commit: `8973412`
- Notes: udl adopts the *idea* of per-site extractor classes with
  `_VALID_URL` matching and a build-time generated lazy stub registry so
  sidecar startup does not import every site module. Adapted from
  `devscripts/make_lazy_extractors.py` and `devscripts/lazy_load_template.py`
  at that commit. No yt-dlp extractor implementations are vendored.

### yt-dlp networking — `core/udl/network/`
- Upstream: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp (`yt_dlp/networking`)
- License: **Unlicense** (public domain dedication)
- Reference commit: `897341241f2bfb2439fe0367f4c7c9ccd29a3828`
- Notes: udl reimplements a slim Request / Response / RequestHandler /
  RequestDirector interface in the same style (urllib, requests, optional
  curl_cffi, optional websockets). This is **not** a copy of yt-dlp sources;
  proxy, User-Agent, and rate limits are centralized in `udl.network`.
  curl_cffi browser impersonation is **opt-in / off by default** (same policy
  as Cloudflare challenge bypass). No paywall, VIP, ToS, or DRM bypass.

